{
    "description": "Merkle inclusion proofs for verify() mode \"merkleProof\". Every SDK must fold `leaf` through `proof` and get `root` exactly when `valid` is true. Roots were computed by merkletreejs 0.5 with { sortPairs: true }, an implementation independent of the SDKs.",
    "format": {
        "hash": "Keccak-256 (the original Keccak, not FIPS-202 SHA3-256)",
        "leaf": "the record hash itself, as returned by hash() — not hashed again",
        "pair": "parent = keccak256(a || b) with the two 32-byte nodes in ascending byte order (OpenZeppelin MerkleProof.verify), so proofs carry no left/right flags",
        "proof": "sibling hashes ordered from the leaf up to the root; in a query result they follow the transaction hash, i.e. proof = [txHash, ...siblings]",
        "oddNodes": "a node without a pair is promoted to the next level unchanged",
        "leaves": "record i is keccak256(\"record-i\") (UTF-8), for i from 0"
    },
